---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHead from '../../components/PageHead.astro';
import AsideLinks from '../../components/doc/AsideLinks.astro';
import AsideCta from '../../components/doc/AsideCta.astro';
import Closing from '../../components/Closing.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/Faq.astro';
import { siteBase } from '../../lib/site';
import { breadcrumb, faqPage } from '../../lib/schema';

const SITE = siteBase(Astro.site);
const path = '/tools/ad-budget-calculator/';
const title = 'Free Ad Budget Calculator for Health Brands | AdBoost Health';
const description = 'Reverse-engineer the monthly ad budget you need to hit a new-customer target at your CAC - with expected revenue and ROAS. Free health-marketing calculator.';
const faq = [
  { q: 'How do I calculate my ad budget?', a: 'Budget = target new customers × CAC. To hit 200 customers at a $150 CAC, you need roughly $30,000 in acquisition spend for the period.' },
  { q: 'Should I budget on CAC or ROAS?', a: 'Plan on CAC and payback for subscription models, since ROAS ignores retention and margin. Use ROAS as a top-line efficiency check, not the target you optimize to.' },
  { q: 'How much creative does that budget need?', a: 'In health, holding benchmark CAC takes 30–60 fresh creatives a month; running 5–10 typically pushes CAC 40–80% over. Budget for creative volume, not just media.' },
];
const jsonLd = [
  breadcrumb(SITE, [{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Tools', href: '/tools/' }, { label: 'Ad Budget Calculator', href: path }]),
  faqPage(faq),
];
---
<BaseLayout {title} {description} canonicalPath={path} {jsonLd}>
  <PageHead label="Free tools" labelHref="/tools/" title="Ad budget calculator" lede="Work backwards from a customer target to the monthly ad budget it takes: with the revenue and ROAS that budget should return." dots />

  <section class="tone-paper page-body" data-nav="paper">
    <div class="wrap doc">
      <div class="doc-main">
      <div class="calc" data-reveal>
        <div class="calc-fields">
          <div class="calc-field">
            <label for="target">Target new customers <span class="hint">(per month)</span></label>
            <div class="calc-input"><input id="target" type="number" inputmode="decimal" value="200" min="0" /></div>
          </div>
          <div class="calc-field">
            <label for="cac3">Target CAC</label>
            <div class="calc-input"><span class="pfx">$</span><input id="cac3" type="number" inputmode="decimal" value="150" min="0" /></div>
          </div>
          <div class="calc-field">
            <label for="aov">Avg. first-order / monthly revenue per customer</label>
            <div class="calc-input"><span class="pfx">$</span><input id="aov" type="number" inputmode="decimal" value="199" min="0" /></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="calc-result gcard">
          <div class="cr-main">
            <div class="cr-label">Monthly ad budget</div>
            <div class="cr-value" id="budgetOut">$30,000</div>
          </div>
          <div class="cr-sub">
            <div><div class="k">EXPECTED REVENUE</div><div class="v" id="revOut">$39,800</div></div>
            <div><div class="k">BLENDED ROAS</div><div class="v" id="roasOut">1.3×</div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="cr-note">Plan on CAC and payback, not ROAS alone - retention decides the real return.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="calc-foot">Runs in your browser. This sizes media at your target CAC; remember health accounts also need budget for 30–60 fresh creatives a month to hold that CAC. Target-CAC and creative-volume ranges come from our <a href="/blog/telehealth-cac-benchmarks-2026/">2026 health-vertical benchmarks</a>.</p>
        <div class="prose">
        <h2>How the ad budget calculation works</h2>
      <p>Your monthly ad budget is a function of two numbers: how many customers you want and what each one costs to acquire. Set the target, use a realistic CAC for your vertical, and the budget follows.</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Set your monthly customer target.</strong> Decide how many new customers or patients you want to acquire this month.</li>
        <li><strong>Enter your target CAC.</strong> Use your current customer acquisition cost, or a <a href="/tools/cac-calculator/">benchmark CAC</a> for your vertical.</li>
        <li><strong>Multiply target by CAC.</strong> Ad budget = target new customers × CAC. 200 customers at a $150 CAC needs about $30,000 in monthly acquisition spend.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>One caveat health brands miss: media is not the whole budget. Holding a benchmark CAC in a policed vertical takes 30-60 fresh, compliant creatives a month; running five to ten typically pushes CAC 40-80% higher. Plan on CAC and payback rather than ROAS - a strong ROAS that ignores retention and margin still loses money in subscription health. Once you have a budget, sanity-check the unit economics with the <a href="/tools/ltv-cac-calculator/">LTV:CAC calculator</a>, and judge the result on <a href="/glossary/blended-cac/">blended CAC</a>, not one platform's claimed number.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-sec" id="faq">
          <h2>FAQ</h2>
          <Faq items={faq} />
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="doc-aside">
        <AsideLinks label="More free tools" links={[{ href: '/tools/cac-calculator/', label: 'CAC calculator' }, { href: '/tools/ltv-cac-calculator/', label: 'LTV:CAC calculator' }, { href: '/blog/telehealth-cac-benchmarks-2026/', label: 'CAC benchmarks by vertical' }]} />
        <AsideCta heading="Plan your next quarter" text="We'll pressure-test your budget and targets against your vertical's benchmarks." />
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Closing />

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      const target = document.getElementById('target');
      const cac = document.getElementById('cac3');
      const aov = document.getElementById('aov');
      const budgetOut = document.getElementById('budgetOut');
      const revOut = document.getElementById('revOut');
      const roasOut = document.getElementById('roasOut');
      const money = (n) => '$' + Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-US');
      function calc() {
        const t = parseFloat(target.value) || 0;
        const c = parseFloat(cac.value) || 0;
        const a = parseFloat(aov.value) || 0;
        const budget = t * c;
        const rev = t * a;
        budgetOut.textContent = money(budget);
        revOut.textContent = money(rev);
        roasOut.textContent = budget > 0 ? (rev / budget).toFixed(1) + '×' : '-';
      }
      [target, cac, aov].forEach((el) => el.addEventListener('input', calc));
      calc();
    })();
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
